    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0247" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710G1A/294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-06T12:00:00-05:00">December 6,
                        1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Your 21, December 2, 9 p.m. I have discussed this with the President. It is
                    our judgment that the proposal is not open to criticism <pb facs="0248" n="160"
                        xml:id="pg160"/> except possibly because you would naturally be forced to
                    include exceptions to cover possible actions by the N. R. A.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d62-f1"/> and the A. A. A.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d62-f2"/> In the
                    light of this fact and the fact that other governments would thereby put forward
                    other exceptions, the proposal could only be valuable from the point of view of
                    expressing ultimate objectives rather than from the point of view of practical
                    and immediate progress.</p>
                <p>It seems to us that all possible emphasis on the immediate undertaking of
                    bilateral negotiations would be more useful during this period of unsettled
                    Government finance and of sharply fluctuating exchanges and we wish to submit
                    this for your consideration.</p>
                <p>The attitude you express in the final sentence of your 27, December 5, seems
                    advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
